# Text is stored with LF and checked out in whatever the platform uses. Without this, a file's
# stored line endings are decided by whichever tool last wrote it, and the two do not have to agree.
# A file stored with CRLF that a script rewrites as LF then reads as every line changed, which turns
# a small edit into a whole-file diff and buries the real change in a review.
#
# That is not hypothetical here. Two plan docs were stored with CRLF, and the larger of them turned
# 268 edited lines into 13,000 twice in one chunk.
#
# Binary content is detected and left alone by the same rule, since auto only converts what has no
# NUL bytes in it.
* text=auto

# Named rather than left to the detection, because a photo fixture that lost its CRs would stop
# being the bytes the test was written against. This repository's test data is real camera output.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.avif binary
*.heic binary
*.webp binary
*.arw binary
*.cr2 binary
*.nef binary
*.ico binary
